WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.896
Hannah: Shadow mode suggests false rejections for office shoppers.

2
00:00:04.896 --> 00:00:09.023
Raj: The working hypothesis is shared-IP bucket collisions.

3
00:00:09.023 --> 00:00:13.247
Lukas: Can you identify legitimate authenticated requests there?

4
00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:18.766
Anika: Yes, separate customers. Their combined traffic hits quotas.

5
00:00:18.766 --> 00:00:22.750
Priya: Just to confirm, expansion pauses, right?

6
00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:27.670
Raj: Yes. The error rate spiked on recommendation canaries.

7
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:32.901
Hannah: Separate deliberate throttling from unexpected server failures.

8
00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:37.413
Anika: Checkout's stable. We can't rule that out later.

9
00:00:37.413 --> 00:00:41.780
Lukas: Maybe identity-based quotas would reduce collateral damage.

10
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.500
Priya: Okay, test that before touching the global ceiling.

